WEBVTT

00:04.754 --> 00:06.551
Oh, man.

00:06.723 --> 00:08.657
That was intense.

00:09.459 --> 00:11.791
I need some fluids.

00:18.835 --> 00:20.860
I must've been down a quart.

00:21.037 --> 00:23.528
Guess that makes you up a quart, huh?

00:24.541 --> 00:27.669
Hey, you know what would be good
right now?

00:27.844 --> 00:29.471
A pudding cup.

00:29.646 --> 00:31.978
I've got some in the fridge.
Ahem. You want one?

00:34.951 --> 00:38.216
Um, you have
a bad experience with pudding?

00:38.788 --> 00:40.653
What are we doing, Charlie?

00:41.224 --> 00:46.059
Well, you're crying, and my best guess
is I'm about to apologize for something.

00:46.229 --> 00:49.221
Every time I come over,
it's the same routine.

00:49.399 --> 00:52.129
We have Chinese takeout,
then we have sex...

00:52.302 --> 00:54.793
...then we roll over and go to sleep.

00:54.971 --> 00:58.134
Which is why I suggested the pudding.

00:59.042 --> 01:02.068
You know, mix it up a little.

01:02.579 --> 01:06.743
Besides, what about all the wonderful
talking and joking and, you know...

01:06.916 --> 01:10.283
- ...sharing we do?
- Sharing?

01:10.687 --> 01:16.148
- What do we share, Charlie?
- Well, uh, we share Chinese takeout.

01:16.326 --> 01:20.092
And, uh, hey, the other night
we watched the Laker game together.

01:20.263 --> 01:23.494
You watched it over my shoulder
while we were having sex.

01:24.200 --> 01:27.101
Oh, come on, it was overtime.

01:27.604 --> 01:30.300
What kind of relationship is this?

01:30.473 --> 01:32.907
We don't go anywhere,
we don't do anything.

01:33.076 --> 01:35.271
Where do you wanna go?
What do you wanna do?

01:35.445 --> 01:40.212
- I can get Laker tickets.
- I don't want to go to a basketball game.

01:40.383 --> 01:44.444
I wanna know who you are.
I want you to know who I am.

01:44.621 --> 01:47.920
- I know who you are.
- You do?

01:48.091 --> 01:49.581
Okay, what's my middle name?

01:50.093 --> 01:51.720
Your middle name?

01:51.895 --> 01:53.260
Okay.

01:53.429 --> 01:55.329
I know this.

01:56.232 --> 01:58.132
- Sunburned boobs.
- What?

01:58.301 --> 02:00.269
Hang on, hang on.

02:00.436 --> 02:04.770
Sunburned boobs, red boobs,
red breasts. Robin.

02:06.976 --> 02:08.466
A little memory trick.

02:08.645 --> 02:10.909
My middle name is Christine.

02:11.848 --> 02:13.110
Not a very good trick.

02:14.350 --> 02:15.942
Who's my best friend?

02:16.119 --> 02:17.279
Where do I work?

02:17.453 --> 02:19.114
What's my cat's name?

02:19.289 --> 02:20.813
What- What's my favorite movie?

02:20.990 --> 02:22.423
What kind of music do I like?

02:22.592 --> 02:23.991
What religion was I raised in?

02:24.160 --> 02:26.287
And do I have any brothers and sisters?

02:27.931 --> 02:30.399
Okay, I'd like to start with the cat.

02:32.902 --> 02:35.268
I'm gonna go with Fluffy.

02:35.772 --> 02:38.002
Drop dead.

02:39.309 --> 02:41.402
Snowball? Mr. Mittens?

02:41.578 --> 02:43.603
Tiger? Whiskers? Puss-Puss?

02:45.315 --> 02:48.910
- Oh, come on, what's my middle name?
Francis.

02:49.085 --> 02:52.316
- No, it's not.
Yes, it is.

02:52.488 --> 02:54.422
Show off.

03:04.234 --> 03:07.101
Oh, Chelsea, come on,
how much do I need to know about you...

03:07.270 --> 03:09.238
...other than I'm crazy about you?

03:09.405 --> 03:12.135
It's not that you don't know,
it's that you don't care.

03:12.609 --> 03:15.601
I do care. I just don't pay close attention.

03:15.778 --> 03:17.040
Goodbye, Charlie.

03:17.213 --> 03:21.206
I mean, uh, I pay attention,
but I don't test well.

03:28.224 --> 03:31.159
What did you do,
bring out the handcuffs too early?

03:32.896 --> 03:36.559
- Apparently, I don't know her middle name.
- It's Christine.

03:37.100 --> 03:38.533
- How do you know?
- She told me.

03:38.701 --> 03:40.328
- Why did she tell you?
- I asked her.

03:40.503 --> 03:43.529
- Why did you ask?
- How else do you get to know a person?

03:43.706 --> 03:45.640
Go away.

03:45.942 --> 03:49.139
Ahem, if a woman stormed out on me
after sex, would you go away?

03:49.312 --> 03:51.439
That's beside the point.

03:52.415 --> 03:54.007
So, what happened?

03:54.183 --> 03:55.741
I don't know.

03:55.919 --> 03:57.216
We were having a nice night.

03:57.387 --> 03:59.878
Little lo mein, little sex,
then the crying started.

04:00.056 --> 04:02.923
Oh, yeah. Been there, done that.

04:03.760 --> 04:06.160
No, she was crying.

04:08.831 --> 04:12.028
- She wants more out of our relationship.
- More what?

04:12.535 --> 04:13.695
I'm not sure.

04:13.870 --> 04:15.838
I know it's not pudding.

04:17.040 --> 04:19.201
Well, what did she say?

04:19.642 --> 04:21.906
She said I don't know her well enough.

04:22.078 --> 04:24.137
You tell me, what's more important
to know:

04:24.314 --> 04:27.909
her cat's name or which of her body parts
you can't sneak up on?

04:28.084 --> 04:30.848
Well, I'm not sure
one necessarily precludes the other.

04:31.020 --> 04:35.923
Yeah, well, I've never been mule-kicked
for not knowing a cat's name.

04:36.960 --> 04:38.188
It doesn't matter.

04:38.361 --> 04:39.885
There's more where she came from.

04:40.630 --> 04:42.530
Speaking of which.

04:43.232 --> 04:45.530
Where does she come from?

04:46.336 --> 04:49.897
- I don't know and I don't care.
- Davenport, Iowa.

04:50.073 --> 04:52.041
Bite me.

04:52.976 --> 04:54.944
- Wanna know her cat's name?
- No.

04:55.478 --> 04:57.446
It's Mandu.

04:59.215 --> 05:02.946
- Mandu?
- Yeah. You know, "Cat Mandu."

05:03.987 --> 05:05.750
It's cute, huh?

05:05.922 --> 05:07.787
Why was I thinking Puss-Puss?

05:08.424 --> 05:10.415
Because that's what
you're always thinking.

05:15.531 --> 05:17.965
What happened to all the pudding cups?

05:18.401 --> 05:22.462
- I guess your uncle ate them.
- All of them? There were two 12-packs.

05:22.939 --> 05:24.566
Have something else.

05:27.377 --> 05:30.107
No cookies?
What the hell is going on around here?

05:30.279 --> 05:33.146
- Hey, watch your mouth.
- I am watching it. It's empty.

05:33.316 --> 05:35.409
I need dessert.

05:37.086 --> 05:39.520
- Son of a bitch.
- Jake.

05:41.190 --> 05:43.784
Frozen peas.
What am I gonna do with frozen peas?

05:43.960 --> 05:46.224
Well, if you want dessert, have an apple.

05:46.396 --> 05:47.522
Not funny, Dad.

05:50.266 --> 05:52.928
You sure I can't interest you
in a pudding cup?

05:53.102 --> 05:55.036
Thanks, I'm okay.

05:55.204 --> 06:00.005
- How about a chocolate chunk cookie?
- No, thank you.

06:01.711 --> 06:04.680
- Did you quit drinking?
- God, no.

06:04.847 --> 06:06.940
- Why?
- You seem to be experimenting...

06:07.116 --> 06:09.175
...with a new sugar-delivery system.

06:11.120 --> 06:13.020
Anything bothering you lately?

06:15.158 --> 06:19.993
Well, there is this one thing, but I don't
know if it's medical or psychological.

06:20.530 --> 06:22.054
Tell me.

06:22.765 --> 06:27.532
Lately, I've passed up a couple
of opportunities to get some strange.

06:28.438 --> 06:29.962
Strange?

06:30.139 --> 06:31.538
Um...

06:32.275 --> 06:35.176
Women with whom
I have not previously been acquainted.

06:35.344 --> 06:37.403
Oh, right, strange.

06:37.580 --> 06:38.979
Charming.

06:39.148 --> 06:40.172
Go on.

06:41.584 --> 06:43.916
I was wondering
if there's something wrong with me.

06:44.087 --> 06:47.250
Because you passed up meaningless sex
with strangers?

06:47.423 --> 06:49.015
Exactly.

06:49.192 --> 06:51.160
That's not like me.

06:51.561 --> 06:55.361
Hey, you know, I bet "strange"
comes from "stranger."

06:56.099 --> 06:57.657
I wouldn't be surprised.

06:59.202 --> 07:01.067
So, what else going on with your life?

07:02.105 --> 07:03.697
Not much.

07:03.873 --> 07:06.535
I've been gaining a little weight
for some reason.

07:07.910 --> 07:12.006
- Maybe I haven't been sleeping well.
- Yeah, that's probably it.

07:15.251 --> 07:18.880
Oh, and this one girl I've been seeing
pretty regularly decided to dump me.

07:19.455 --> 07:20.979
Huh.

07:21.657 --> 07:23.420
- "Huh," what?
- Oh, nothing.

07:23.593 --> 07:27.461
It's just, sometimes I feel like
I'm stealing your money.

07:27.630 --> 07:30.030
So tell me about this woman.

07:30.466 --> 07:31.933
Chelsea?

07:32.101 --> 07:33.398
Not much to tell.

07:33.569 --> 07:36.766
She's beautiful, sexy,
smart, independent.

07:38.207 --> 07:41.335
Sometimes, when she laughs,
she makes a little snorting noise.

07:41.511 --> 07:43.411
It's really cute. Kind of like:

07:47.984 --> 07:50.043
Not as cute when I do it.

07:50.786 --> 07:51.980
Sounds like quite a catch.

07:52.455 --> 07:54.582
- She's okay.
- Why did she dump you?

07:54.757 --> 07:57.317
Who can understand a woman's mind?

07:58.561 --> 08:01.394
Yeah, we're pretty little puzzles,
ain't we?

08:02.031 --> 08:03.430
So it's not just me.

08:06.602 --> 08:11.062
Anyway, for some reason, she suddenly
became dissatisfied with our relationship.

08:11.240 --> 08:14.107
- Well, describe the relationship.
- It was great.

08:14.277 --> 08:16.472
She'd come over a couple times a week.

08:16.646 --> 08:19.342
Either she'd bring food
or I'd have something delivered.

08:19.515 --> 08:20.777
We'd have sex, then eat...

08:20.950 --> 08:23.942
...then maybe have sex again
depending on what was on TV.

08:24.387 --> 08:27.288
And she became dissatisfied with that?

08:27.890 --> 08:29.323
I know, right?

08:31.861 --> 08:34.193
Ooh, butterscotch.

08:34.630 --> 08:37.360
So how did you feel about losing her?

08:37.533 --> 08:39.592
- What do you mean?
- What do I mean?

08:39.769 --> 08:43.705
Come on, Charlie,
Dr. Seuss could diagnose this.

08:43.873 --> 08:47.707
You're stuffing yourself with crap
to suppress your negative feelings.

08:48.544 --> 08:50.603
No, I'm pretty sure that's why I drink.

08:51.547 --> 08:52.878
You have a choice here.

08:53.049 --> 08:55.347
You can dig down
and confront your feelings...

08:55.518 --> 08:57.782
...so they won't be
controlling your behavior...

08:57.954 --> 09:00.149
...or you can keep
eating pudding and cookies...

09:00.323 --> 09:03.019
...until you have more chins
than a Chinese phone book.

09:04.460 --> 09:05.688
Hmm...

09:05.861 --> 09:07.021
No. What else you got?

09:07.997 --> 09:11.489
- Do you have a better idea?
- What if I could get Chelsea back?

09:11.667 --> 09:14.295
That would only be a temporary solution.

09:14.470 --> 09:16.734
So? That's what people said
about bourbon...

09:16.906 --> 09:19.340
...and we've been together
for almost 30 years.

09:19.508 --> 09:24.172
Okay, you're right. Go get Chelsea back,
and all your problems will be solved.

09:24.614 --> 09:29.813
- I'm sensing sarcasm.
- Oh, good, we're finally making progress.

09:35.291 --> 09:37.282
Here you go.

09:37.560 --> 09:38.925
What are you drinking?

09:39.095 --> 09:42.587
Chocolate caramel frappuccino
with whipped cream and sprinkles.

09:44.867 --> 09:47.995
My nephew turned me on to it.
You want some?

09:48.170 --> 09:51.162
No, thanks, I had a hot-fudge sundae
for breakfast.

09:51.340 --> 09:53.433
Ooh, that sounds good.

09:59.015 --> 10:01.210
Ah, you look nice.

10:03.719 --> 10:06.517
I've gotta get back to work, Charlie.
What do you want?

10:06.822 --> 10:08.949
I just wanted to see you,
see how you're doing.

10:09.125 --> 10:11.286
- I'm fine.
- Good.

10:11.460 --> 10:15.191
And how's your family
back in Davenport, Iowa?

10:15.364 --> 10:17.229
I'm from Champaign, Illinois.

10:20.136 --> 10:22.263
- You sure?
- I'm sure.

10:22.938 --> 10:25.133
Bastard set me up.

10:26.075 --> 10:29.169
- What?
- Nothing, nothing.

10:29.345 --> 10:33.475
- I miss you.
- I miss you too, but it doesn't matter.

10:33.649 --> 10:37.141
Our relationship wasn't going anywhere,
and you are incapable of change.

10:37.320 --> 10:40.551
It's not that I'm incapable,
I've just been unwilling.

10:41.257 --> 10:44.420
- Thanks for clearing that up.
- No, no, no. Wait, wait, wait.

10:44.860 --> 10:46.122
I've been seeing a shrink.

10:46.796 --> 10:48.923
- Really?
- Yeah. I'm making a lot of progress...

10:49.098 --> 10:51.965
...confronting my-
What do you call them? Personal issues.

10:53.402 --> 10:57.168
- Well, I'm glad to hear it.
- Come, sit.

11:00.810 --> 11:03.973
And check this out, the shrink's a woman.
A real ballbuster.

11:04.146 --> 11:06.808
- I can't get away with anything.
- Ballbuster?

11:07.516 --> 11:11.612
In a good way.
You know, a buster of emotional balls.

11:13.923 --> 11:15.652
You should meet her.

11:16.492 --> 11:18.619
Are you suggesting
we go to couples counseling?

11:20.529 --> 11:21.860
Uh...

11:25.568 --> 11:27.297
Sure.

11:27.903 --> 11:30.838
I mean, I wanna work on our relationship,
and what better way...

11:31.006 --> 11:32.837
...than couples counseling?

11:33.809 --> 11:36.300
- You're serious?
- Of course I'm serious.

11:36.479 --> 11:39.676
You think I'd blurt out something like that
in a desperate attempt...

11:39.849 --> 11:41.783
...to keep you from leaving?

11:42.485 --> 11:45.579
- It occurred to me.
- Well, clearly you don't know me...

11:45.755 --> 11:47.746
- ...as well as you should.
- All right.

11:47.923 --> 11:51.290
Couples counseling.
Wow. I'm impressed, Charlie.

11:51.460 --> 11:53.394
Ha, ha. Me too.

11:54.497 --> 11:56.522
Okay, I gotta run.

11:56.732 --> 11:59.132
- Let me know when our appointment is.
- Sure thing.

11:59.668 --> 12:01.226
Bye-bye.

12:03.406 --> 12:06.034
Oh, God, what have I done?

12:15.684 --> 12:18.312
Davenport, Iowa?

12:19.755 --> 12:23.555
Oh, uh, did I say Davenport, Iowa?

12:23.726 --> 12:25.921
I meant Champaign, Illinois.

12:26.862 --> 12:30.525
- Okay, that's one for you.
- Thank you.

12:32.568 --> 12:34.001
Ow!

12:35.604 --> 12:37.663
And that's one for me.

12:38.607 --> 12:40.575
Now, I need some advice.

12:40.743 --> 12:42.574
Oh, and just a friendly heads-up...

12:42.745 --> 12:45.213
...you screw with me,
it's gonna cost you some teeth.

12:45.381 --> 12:46.905
I'm listening.

12:47.082 --> 12:50.051
Wait a minute, what's this about?

12:51.053 --> 12:52.850
Oh, he bought some stuff
with his own money...

12:53.022 --> 12:56.185
- ...and he doesn't want you eating it.
- Huh.

13:00.896 --> 13:04.059
- You've been to couples counseling, right?
- Yeah, why?

13:04.233 --> 13:07.930
I'm going with Chelsea,
and I need to know what I'm getting into.

13:08.137 --> 13:10.071
Oh, you're gonna love it.

13:10.773 --> 13:13.264
- I am?
- Absolutely.

13:13.509 --> 13:17.104
Once a week, you sit on a couch
with your significant other...

13:17.279 --> 13:22.182
...while she snips off your testicles,
reaches up inside your chest cavity...

13:22.351 --> 13:24.182
...and goes like this:

13:25.688 --> 13:26.985
To your heart.

13:29.058 --> 13:33.154
- That doesn't sound very good.
- Oh, it's horrible.

13:33.496 --> 13:34.554
But it's worth it...

13:34.730 --> 13:37.324
...because you're paying a stranger
to watch...

13:37.500 --> 13:39.661
...while your life goes down
the toilet...

13:41.337 --> 13:44.568
...along with your money
and your house and your car...

13:44.740 --> 13:48.301
...and every last shred
of your self-respect!

13:52.214 --> 13:54.580
You know,
maybe you're not the right guy to ask.

13:55.017 --> 13:58.145
Oh, no, no, no.
I'm the perfect guy to ask.

13:58.320 --> 14:02.120
Uh, when Judith and I started, ha, ha,
we were just a couple with a few problems.

14:02.291 --> 14:05.658
When we finished,
I came to live on your couch!

14:07.897 --> 14:10.798
God bless couples counseling!

14:17.373 --> 14:19.341
That better not be
one of my pudding cups.

14:24.847 --> 14:26.337
Nope, ahem.

14:41.463 --> 14:45.126
- Hi, Charlie. Come on in.
- Shouldn't we wait for Chelsea?

14:45.301 --> 14:46.393
She's already here.

14:47.236 --> 14:48.567
Really?

14:48.737 --> 14:50.864
That seems a little ambush-y.

14:52.007 --> 14:54.532
- Hi, sweetie.
- You're late.

14:54.710 --> 14:57.304
I know, I know. I'm sorry.

14:57.479 --> 15:00.642
But, ahem, I have a good excuse.

15:01.784 --> 15:03.979
Happy first day of counseling.

15:04.687 --> 15:07.053
- You brought a present?
- Yeah.

15:07.222 --> 15:09.349
- Isn't that the protocol?
- No.

15:10.359 --> 15:14.193
So you don't want
this bottle of champagne?

15:16.231 --> 15:18.597
Bastard got me again.

15:19.168 --> 15:22.331
- Why don't we get started?
- Hold on. Hold on.

15:22.972 --> 15:25.907
Does the name Mandu
ring any kind of a bell?

15:26.842 --> 15:30.243
- What?
- I'm gonna kill him.

15:31.046 --> 15:35.483
Why don't we start out with
why we're here and what our goals are?

15:35.651 --> 15:39.109
- Chelsea, would you like to go first?
- Sure.

15:39.455 --> 15:44.688
I want to know if my relationship
with Charlie can be more than sex, TV...

15:44.860 --> 15:46.555
...and Chinese food.

15:46.729 --> 15:49.721
- It can. Right, doc?
- Of course it can.

15:49.898 --> 15:51.525
Thank you.

15:51.700 --> 15:54.032
Well, this is good. This is progress.

15:54.570 --> 15:56.970
I have to say,
this has been a very good session.

15:57.139 --> 15:59.266
Where do you think you're going?

15:59.675 --> 16:01.142
Nowhere.

16:02.311 --> 16:05.508
Just stretching my legs.

16:07.449 --> 16:10.907
Charlie, before you got here,
Chelsea mentioned that she feels...

16:11.086 --> 16:14.920
- ...you've fallen into a rut.
- A rut? We're not in a rut.

16:15.090 --> 16:16.887
When's the last time
we did something new?

16:18.427 --> 16:20.327
Hello.

16:23.666 --> 16:25.293
Great. What else?

16:26.268 --> 16:27.565
Uh...

16:29.238 --> 16:30.262
He's got nothing.

16:30.973 --> 16:34.670
Excuse me. If this is gonna work, you can't
jump all over me while I'm thinking.

16:34.943 --> 16:37.935
- I'm sorry. Go ahead.
- Thank you.

16:41.884 --> 16:43.476
I got nothing.

16:44.787 --> 16:47.255
Okay, might I make a suggestion?

16:47.423 --> 16:53.055
Would you be willing to commit to Chelsea
that maybe once a week, twice a month...

16:53.228 --> 16:56.425
...you do something together
completely outside your comfort zone?

16:56.598 --> 16:58.293
Done, no problem.

16:58.934 --> 17:00.925
So we could go to the ballet...

17:01.103 --> 17:04.402
...the opera, visit my parents,
hang out with my brother...

17:04.573 --> 17:06.939
- ...go hiking with my friends?
- Yeah, whoa, whoa.

17:07.109 --> 17:11.205
I was thinking more like renting a chick flick
and ordering Italian.

17:11.947 --> 17:14.313
- This is hopeless.
- No, no, no, there's hope.

17:14.483 --> 17:16.610
There's always hope. Keep hope alive.

17:18.487 --> 17:19.681
I can do those things.

17:21.123 --> 17:23.683
Come. Sit.

17:32.334 --> 17:34.268
Charlie, has it ever occurred to you...

17:34.436 --> 17:37.371
...that you might enjoy doing new things
and meeting new people?

17:38.841 --> 17:42.800
I know I'm supposed
to say yes, but, uh...

17:43.879 --> 17:48.748
...every fiber of my body
is screaming, "No!"

17:50.986 --> 17:52.920
All right, then I have to ask.

17:53.088 --> 17:56.455
Given that you and Chelsea
are such different people...

17:56.625 --> 17:58.820
...why do you want to be
in this relationship?

18:00.295 --> 18:01.762
Well...

18:02.531 --> 18:04.192
...because I'm crazy about her.

18:04.366 --> 18:06.732
When I'm with somebody else,
I'm thinking of her.

18:06.902 --> 18:09.871
Not that I've been with anybody else.
Tell her, doc.

18:10.038 --> 18:11.505
He passed up strange.

18:12.841 --> 18:16.208
See? That's gotta mean something,
considering how I used to, you know...

18:16.378 --> 18:18.312
...live for strange.

18:18.480 --> 18:21.278
First time in the sack,
she was the strange.

18:22.017 --> 18:24.247
Charlie, can I give you my opinion
as your therapist?

18:24.419 --> 18:26.250
- Sure.
- Shut up.

18:27.489 --> 18:29.923
Oh, God, I wish I could.

18:30.726 --> 18:34.184
Chelsea, look. I know I'm not perfect.

18:34.363 --> 18:36.524
- Ha, ha.
- Hey, hey, hey.

18:37.232 --> 18:39.928
I'm sorry.
That was probably unprofessional.

18:41.236 --> 18:46.071
Anyway, you need to know
that you mean everything to me...

18:46.241 --> 18:48.903
...and I'll do whatever it takes
to make this work.

18:49.344 --> 18:51.403
- You really mean that?
- I do.

18:52.347 --> 18:53.371
Thank you, Charlie.

18:55.551 --> 18:58.884
Well, this has been very helpful.

18:59.054 --> 19:01.522
Sit down, Charlie.

19:01.857 --> 19:02.949
We're not done?

19:03.125 --> 19:05.218
Not even close.

19:05.794 --> 19:06.988
Oh, boy.

19:07.162 --> 19:09.630
What else could we possibly
have to talk about?

19:09.798 --> 19:12.699
Well, there's always your mother
and that your relationship issues...

19:12.868 --> 19:16.929
...are linked to anger towards her
as well as fear of your latent homosexuality.

19:19.708 --> 19:21.801
It was kind of a rhetorical question.

19:34.122 --> 19:37.216
Charlie?
- Yeah.

19:37.392 --> 19:40.054
How was couples counseling?

19:43.298 --> 19:44.822
You really wanna know?

19:52.708 --> 19:56.041
Sure. Tell me everything.

19:59.414 --> 20:00.847
Ow!

20:01.884 --> 20:03.044
Why?

20:03.218 --> 20:04.310
Why would you do that?

20:04.853 --> 20:07.583
You know, I- I've been asking myself
the same thing...

20:07.756 --> 20:11.590
...and the only thing I can come up with is,
it's really, really funny.

20:13.428 --> 20:16.329
Go ahead, yuck it up.

20:16.598 --> 20:20.227
Those were among the worst 50 minutes
of my entire life.

20:20.402 --> 20:24.668
- I told you, didn't I tell you?
- Yep, you told me.

20:24.840 --> 20:27.866
I bet you left with your gonads
in a guppy bag.

20:28.310 --> 20:30.870
- I didn't get a bag.
- Going back next week?

20:31.046 --> 20:32.104
Uh-huh.

20:32.281 --> 20:34.044
- Hundred-eighty dollars an hour?
- Two forty.

20:34.216 --> 20:36.582
Ooh, licensed.

20:38.954 --> 20:41.218
You two kids will patch things up
in no time.

20:41.390 --> 20:45.087
Counseling didn't help your relationships.
Doesn't mean it won't help mine.

20:45.527 --> 20:49.429
Right, right.
Keep drinking that old Kool-Aid.

20:49.898 --> 20:51.263
Looking for something?

20:56.605 --> 20:58.732
Don't screw with me, kid.

20:59.741 --> 21:02.141
Now, hand over the pudding,
or you'll be sorry.

21:02.778 --> 21:03.972
Have an apple.

21:09.651 --> 21:11.118
Little turd called my bluff.

21:18.327 --> 21:19.658
Ow!
